1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,287
Welcome back!

2
00:00:01,287 --> 00:00:06,308
In this lesson, we'll use three reports
that answer the questions every owner asks.

3
00:00:06,308 --> 00:00:07,942
Are we answering the phone?

4
00:00:07,942 --> 00:00:09,394
Are patients turning up?

5
00:00:09,394 --> 00:00:11,875
And how is each person on the team doing?

6
00:00:12,725 --> 00:00:15,065
Let's start with Call Reporting.

7
00:00:15,065 --> 00:00:19,086
It counts every call through
your Kyntlo phone numbers.

8
00:00:19,086 --> 00:00:22,084
In the last 30 days there were 128 calls.

9
00:00:22,084 --> 00:00:24,863
104 were answered, and 24 were missed.

10
00:00:25,713 --> 00:00:28,275
Answer rate is the share you picked up.

11
00:00:28,275 --> 00:00:30,574
81% is good, but look at the chart.

12
00:00:30,574 --> 00:00:36,092
Missed calls peak on Wednesdays, and on
Saturdays more than a quarter go unanswered.

13
00:00:36,092 --> 00:00:40,428
Those are the moments to cover,
or to send an automatic text back.

14
00:00:41,279 --> 00:00:45,101
Calls by source shows which tracking
number each call came in on.

15
00:00:45,101 --> 00:00:49,628
Give your website, your Google ads and
your Google Business Profile their own

16
00:00:49,628 --> 00:00:53,390
numbers, and you'll know exactly
which one makes the phone ring.

17
00:00:53,390 --> 00:00:57,330
You set up those tracking numbers
in Settings, under Phone Numbers.

18
00:00:58,181 --> 00:01:00,860
Below is every call, with who handled it.

19
00:01:00,860 --> 00:01:04,192
If call recording is on,
press play to listen back.

20
00:01:04,192 --> 00:01:06,609
It's the best training tool you have.

21
00:01:06,609 --> 00:01:10,791
Use the filter at the top to see
only inbound or outbound calls.

22
00:01:11,665 --> 00:01:13,863
Next, the Appointment Report.

23
00:01:13,863 --> 00:01:15,986
38 appointments were booked.

24
00:01:15,986 --> 00:01:19,700
33 patients showed up, 3
didn’t, and 2 cancelled.

25
00:01:19,700 --> 00:01:21,670
That’s a show rate of 92%.

26
00:01:22,770 --> 00:01:25,705
The chart breaks each
week down by outcome.

27
00:01:25,705 --> 00:01:31,030
On the right, you can see how appointments
were booked: 24 through your online

28
00:01:31,030 --> 00:01:36,491
booking widget, 9 by staff, and 5 by your
AI agent, often outside opening hours.

29
00:01:37,340 --> 00:01:39,247
Scroll down for each calendar.

30
00:01:39,247 --> 00:01:42,996
Filter to a single calendar,
like the Invisalign free scan,

31
00:01:42,996 --> 00:01:45,093
and you'll see its own show rate.

32
00:01:45,093 --> 00:01:48,207
Free appointments usually
have the most no-shows,

33
00:01:48,207 --> 00:01:50,559
so they need the strongest reminders.

34
00:01:51,410 --> 00:01:55,166
Finally, Agent Reporting shows
each team member side by side.

35
00:01:55,166 --> 00:01:58,860
You'll see the opportunities
they own, how many they've won,

36
00:01:58,860 --> 00:02:02,493
the value of those wins, and
their calls, texts and emails.

37
00:02:03,342 --> 00:02:04,428
Read it fairly.

38
00:02:04,428 --> 00:02:07,107
Priya has won the most, worth £4,250.

39
00:02:07,107 --> 00:02:11,596
James hasn’t closed a deal yet,
but he handled the most calls.

40
00:02:11,596 --> 00:02:16,375
He looks after check-ups, which
rarely become big treatment deals.

41
00:02:16,375 --> 00:02:18,765
Use this for coaching, not blame.

42
00:02:19,615 --> 00:02:24,500
The last column is the average first
reply: how long a new message waits for a

43
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:25,314
human answer.

44
00:02:25,314 --> 00:02:28,758
In sales, speed matters more
than almost anything else.

45
00:02:28,758 --> 00:02:32,766
A lead who hears back within
minutes is far more likely to book.

46
00:02:32,766 --> 00:02:36,461
If one person is much slower,
look at their workload first.

47
00:02:37,314 --> 00:02:38,393
Here's a pro tip.

48
00:02:38,393 --> 00:02:42,838
Every Monday, spend ten minutes on
these three reports with your team.

49
00:02:42,838 --> 00:02:46,458
Look at missed calls, no-shows,
and one win to celebrate.

50
00:02:46,458 --> 00:02:51,220
Small, regular check-ins change habits
far more than a big monthly meeting.

51
00:02:52,073 --> 00:02:53,769
That's the end of Module 2!

52
00:02:53,769 --> 00:02:56,469
You can now read every
report that matters.

53
00:02:56,469 --> 00:03:00,865
In Module 3, we'll dive into Contacts,
starting with the contact list.

54
00:03:00,865 --> 00:03:01,744
See you there.
